## 8. Acceptance — machine signal + glass gate per surface

### [CXC-CAN-VERIFY] Two-tier verdicts — every human-perceptible surface carries a glass gate

- definition: each requirement carries a machine signal (`verify.machine`) AND, for a human-perceptible surface, an explicit human/glass gate (`verify.human`). A machine-green build whose gauges nobody watched move is not accepted.

| ID | Requirement | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|----|-------------|----------------|----------------------|
| CAN-C1 | Raw Layer-1 shape + eff-not-magnitude ([CXC-CAN-RAW], [CXC-CAN-FRAME]) | `test_raw_frame_namespace` asserts `can/<bus>/<hex>` publishes `{id,eff,dlc,data,t}` with `json` engine; a 0x123 standard and a 0x00000123 extended frame publish distinct `(namespace,eff)` and are NOT merged by magnitude | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C2 | RTR/error/over-DLC frames dropped at the reader ([CXC-CAN-FRAME]) | `test_frame_filter` asserts injected RTR, error, and DLC>8 frames publish on NEITHER layer and are logged, not raised | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C3 | stdlib SocketCAN reader works with zero third-party imports, behind the mockcan seam ([CXC-CAN-SOCKETCAN]) | `test_socketcan_reader` (macOS CI, `MockCanBus`) asserts `(arb,eff,data)` decode of standard + extended frames with NO python-can import; a decoder run yields the right `fiat/*` value | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C4 | Two evaluators, one golden ([CXC-CAN-DECODER]) | `test_decoder_python_golden` + the C++ `twai_decoder_crosscheck` decode the same synthetic frame against the same map to the IDENTICAL engineering value; a divergence fails the build; big/little byte_order both covered | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C5 | bridge.py migration byte-identical; LGPL dep gone ([CXC-CAN-BRIDGE-MIGRATE], [CXC-CAN-LICENSE]) | on real `can0`, the ComposeBus-over-CAN round-trip is byte-identical to pre-migration; macOS CI green under `mockcan`; a dependency scan of the installed bridge finds NO LGPL package; P1-5 struck | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C6 | No SIGABRT on unexpected vehicle data ([CXC-CAN-JSON-RULE]) | `test_enum_out_of_domain` injects an unmapped enum index + an empty init value and asserts the process does NOT abort (no ValueError into callback); the signal retains its last valid value or drops with a warning | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C7 | Decoder-map schema validation ([CXC-CAN-DECODER-SCHEMA]) | `test_map_load` asserts: missing required field -> load error naming the entry; both scale/offset AND map -> rejected; `enum` without `map` -> rejected; start_bit/length overrun dlc -> rejected; empty `signals:[]` -> loads, decodes nothing | n/a (structural) |
| CAN-C8 | Tier-agnostic producers — RPi and ESP32 publishes are indistinguishable ([CXC-CAN-CONTRACT]) | a test subscribes `fiat/soc` and asserts identical consumer behavior whether an RPi SocketCAN reader or an ESP32 TWAI reader published it | on glass: the carousel Fiat SOC/SPEED gauges move live and IDENTICALLY off an RPi-published vs an ESP32-published `fiat/*` — an observer cannot tell which board is the source |
| CAN-C9 | Foreign path is RX-only ([CXC-CAN-LOOPGUARD]) | `test_foreign_rx_only` asserts a foreign decoder configuration opens no TX path; on ESP32 the driver installs `TWAI_MODE_LISTEN_ONLY` | on glass: an ESP32 plugged into a LIVE vehicle bus perturbs nothing (LISTEN_ONLY — no ACK transmitted) |
| CAN-C10 | Acceptance filter narrows the firehose ([CXC-CAN-SOCKETCAN], [CXC-CAN-TWAI]) | `test_acceptance_filter` asserts a SocketCAN `CAN_RAW_FILTER` (and a TWAI hardware mask) delivers ONLY the decoder-map frame ids to userspace/the reactive loop | n/a (structural) |

- see-also: [CXC-CAN-CONTRACT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-CAN]

